{"title":"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 8","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<figure class=\"mw-halign-right\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:2006_CyMO-8.PNG\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/10/2006_CyMO-8.PNG/250px-2006_CyMO-8.PNG\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"250\" height=\"234\" class=\"mw-file-element\" srcset=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/10/2006_CyMO-8.PNG/375px-2006_CyMO-8.PNG 1.5x, https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/thumb/1/10/2006_CyMO-8.PNG/500px-2006_CyMO-8.PNG 2x\" /></a><figcaption></figcaption></figure>\n<p>In the figure <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/4/9/249a698122781191eca47fb1948c7a2a8f7e486f.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB\\Gamma \\Delta E$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"69\" height=\"13\" /> is a regular 5-sided polygon and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/e/a/3ead47fb9fb4a4c273feee398f72ff2a09702b84.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$Z$\" width=\"13\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/1/9/b1902d279ba37d60bdce4e0e987b7cd19d48974e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$H$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"18\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/3/2/a321d1b883ba985b1f59ca076beaaf17aa8ab06c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/2/7/027f4a11d6090f9eac0ce2488df6384dad1263ea.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$I$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/f/b/dfb064112b6c94470339f6571f69d07afc1c024c.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$K$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"19\" height=\"14\" /> are the points of intersections of the extensions of the sides.\nIf the area of the \"star\" <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/a/c/7ac77e820ec42bed0956b3870fb23c18b01dc188.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AHB\\Theta \\Gamma I\\Delta KEZA$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"153\" height=\"13\" /> is 1, then the area of the shaded quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/c/b4cb2e8fe8fcfd60365c51b2c1a415e99f0acdf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A\\Gamma IZ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> is\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/b/0/cb0ec4ddfec2fe2d31f9f34f6d63a468b3a2f649.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\mathrm{(A)}\\ \\frac{2}{3}\\qquad\\mathrm{(B)}\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\qquad\\mathrm{(C)}\\ \\frac{3}{7}\\qquad\\mathrm{(D)}\\ \\frac{3}{10}\\qquad\\mathrm{(E)}\\ \\text{None of these}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"457\" height=\"38\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>In the quadrilateral <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/c/b4cb2e8fe8fcfd60365c51b2c1a415e99f0acdf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A\\Gamma IZ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" />, we have three isosceles triangles <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/1/3/c13fcdeb924911a99a3030030e036999e855b239.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A\\Gamma\\Delta$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/d/c3d349cb222846a6e3b8667cb9566139461f9e00.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AZE$\" width=\"41\" height=\"13\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/0/c208d5774fa642a735b01ca7b3ea777a4bdca862.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\Gamma \\Delta I$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"36\" height=\"13\" />. Those are congruent to each other, as well as <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/2/3d236c0041096d5ac15dc3f387134977b786d5fa.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HAB$\" width=\"44\" height=\"13\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/0/a/7/0a7f49d6c5339e79681ced4cb24c84029acc8d8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$B\\Gamma\\Theta$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"42\" height=\"14\" />, and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/8/4a88556627d9084622921b9ade7ee0b3047e40e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EK\\Delta$\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />. Also, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/d/9/1d97cde13496f0e5bd241e37a4cd433ce3a398f3.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AE\\Delta$\" width=\"42\" height=\"13\" /> is congruent to <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/3/6/4369ccb938d86d296fe34bff83b078419be8aaf9.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AB\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"39\" height=\"13\" />. Thus we have two figures of equal area: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/4/c/b4cb2e8fe8fcfd60365c51b2c1a415e99f0acdf5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$A\\Gamma IZ$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> and a combination of two figures: <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/7/9/8/798535e310af0e38d2f79309cec719e9a11be012.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$HB\\Theta\\Gamma A$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"70\" height=\"13\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/a/8/4a88556627d9084622921b9ade7ee0b3047e40e7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$EK\\Delta$\" width=\"45\" height=\"13\" />. Since the area of the whole star is 1, the area of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/2/3/c234ab667a4b37d100fb891e396a348bd104a5e1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$AZI\\Gamma$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"48\" height=\"13\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/8/5/e85dfa8c035f21ee38aed9caab403c04e13771c1.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{1}{2}\\mathrm{(B)}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"38\" height=\"37\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_also\">See also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_8&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"clear:both; margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; align:center; width:60%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum\">2006 Cyprus MO, Lyceum</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problems\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problems\">Problems</a></b>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_7\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 7\">Problem 7</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_9\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 9\">Problem 9</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_1\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_2\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2006_Cyprus_MO/Lyceum/Problem_3\" title=\"2006 Cyprus MO/Lyceum/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php